From: zhzy0077 <zhzy0077@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: calibrate Gaokun3 speaker playback gain

Match the tested 150% PipeWire output at 100% desktop volume on Gaokun3.
Apply the equivalent 27/8 linear gain (+10.57 dB) to the DSP volume control
of graph 1, which both Gaokun3 topologies use for MultiMedia2 speakers.
Leave other machines, headphones, microphones and DP paths unchanged.
Keep the mixer-visible gain and the existing codec/PA limits unchanged.
Clamp the result to the unsigned Q13 parameter range and preserve mute.

This is a local board calibration, not an implementation of Windows
Histen processing or active speaker protection. Software amplification
and DSP amplification occur at different points in the signal chain;
post-boot playback verification is required before considering it deployed.

Signed-off-by: zhzy0077 <zhzy0077@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@
 // Copyright (c) 2020, Linaro Limited
 
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
+#include <linux/limits.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/soc/qcom/apr.h>
 #include <sound/soc.h>
@@ -1212,6 +1214,25 @@
 	return audioreach_graph_send_cmd_sync(graph, pkt, 0);
 }
 
+/* Gaokun3's topology routes graph 1 (MultiMedia2) to the built-in speakers. */
+static u16 audioreach_playback_gain(const struct audioreach_module *module,
+				    u16 gain)
+{
+	const struct audioreach_graph_info *info;
+
+	info = module->container->sub_graph->info;
+	if (!of_machine_is_compatible("huawei,gaokun3") || info->id != 1)
+		return gain;
+
+	/*
+	 * Match PulseAudio/PipeWire's 150% volume at the normal 100% setting:
+	 * 1.5^3 = 27/8 linear gain, or +10.57 dB. Keep the mixer-visible
+	 * gain unchanged and retain the codec/PA protection limits.
+	 * Saturate to the DSP parameter's unsigned Q13 range.
+	 */
+	return min_t(u32, (u32)gain * 27 / 8, U16_MAX);
+}
+
 int audioreach_gain_set_vol_ctrl(struct q6apm *apm,
 				 const struct audioreach_module *module, int vol)
 {
@@ -1233,7 +1254,7 @@
 
 	p = p + APM_MODULE_PARAM_DATA_SIZE;
 	cfg = p;
-	cfg->master_gain =  vol;
+	cfg->master_gain = audioreach_playback_gain(module, vol);
 	return q6apm_send_cmd_sync(apm, pkt, 0);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(audioreach_gain_set_vol_ctrl);
